From: mxreyer <236478497+mxreyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] reduce: barrier after reading the fallback reduction's result

REDUCE_USING_OP (the CUSTOM_REDUCE / pre-2.0 path) ends with every
work-item reading my_reduce[0] after the last barrier of the tree. Nothing
stops work-item 0 from running ahead into the next reduction and writing
my_reduce[0] = myval before the slower work-items have read the previous
result. Any kernel that reduces twice in a row hits it: softmax reduces
max then sum, and softmax_with_loss, bn_sums, global_pooling and the
depthwise backward-filter kernel reduce twice as well.

The softmax and log_softmax unit tests fail with CUSTOM_REDUCE=1 without
this; with it they pass. One extra barrier per reduction; the OpenCL 2.0
work_group_reduce_* path is unaffected.
---
 src/kernels/reduce.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/kernels/reduce.h b/src/kernels/reduce.h
index 0d4bce8..2c62e01 100644
--- a/src/kernels/reduce.h
+++ b/src/kernels/reduce.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
             barrier(CLK_LOCAL_MEM_FENCE); \
         } \
         myval = my_reduce[0]; \
+        barrier(CLK_LOCAL_MEM_FENCE); /* next reduction may overwrite my_reduce[0] before slow work-items read it */ \
     } while(0)
 
 #define REDUCE_OP_ADD(x,y) ((x) + (y))
-- 
2.55.0

